{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/index.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/architecture.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/agents-block.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/index.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/architecture/stack.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/agents-block.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/index.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/architecture.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/agents-block.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/index.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/architecture/stack.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/agents-block.md'","aggregated_output":"Purpose: rules for `index.md`. Template: `assets/index.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `product`, the product name; `docs-format`, the template version the project uses; `issue-tracker`, optional, the address a ticket key is appended to, such as `https://example.atlassian.net/browse/`, deleted when the team has none.\n\nWhat it is: who uses the product and for what, in 2 to 4 sentences, in the user's words. Not a feature list.\n\nDomains: a table with at least one row: domain, what it covers, owner. docs-init asks for the first row. spec-start and docs-map add a row the moment a new domain is named, before any go is asked. The owner is who says go for that domain; on a solo project, that is the user. A domain's behavior lives at `behavior/<domain>/`, so there is no link column.\n\nBehavior: one line pointing at `behavior/`, so an agent that loads only what index.md links to finds the claims. Architecture: one line pointing at `architecture/`.\n\nNothing else: details of any domain belong in behavior/.\nPurpose: rules for `architecture/<area>.md`. Templates: `assets/architecture/<area>.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `area`, the area name. A title, then the area's own table or list. Current state only: no history, no plans. The why links to decision records.\n\nArea files are created the first time they have content, never empty. `stack.md` exists from init, with the commands spec-build and spec-ship run. The folder listing is its own index.\n\n| Area | Holds |\n| --- | --- |\n| `stack` | languages and frameworks, and the commands to install, run, test, lint and build |\n| `conventions` | only the rules agents get wrong without being told: naming, error handling, test style |\n| `boundaries` | modules: name, path, domain, what each may depend on |\n| `data-model` | entities: name, key fields, relations |\n| `contracts` | APIs and events: name, kind, input, output, consumers |\n| `integrations` | external services: purpose, direction, auth, what the product does when it fails |\n| `config` | settings and flags: name, purpose, default, where it's set; never real secret values |\n| `invariants` | non-negotiable rules every spec must keep: ID, rule, why |\n\nWritten by docs-map for what a domain needs, and by spec-ship for the files plan.md lists under Architecture to update at ship.\nPurpose: rules for the project-memory block in the root AGENTS.md. Template: `assets/agents-block.md`.\n\nThe block sits between `<!-- project-memory:start -->` and `<!-- project-memory:end -->` markers, written and refreshed by docs-init only. Everything outside the markers is the project's own and is never touched. The block is root-only; nested AGENTS.md files are named by docs-init, not written.\n\nSlots: `{{docs-path}}` is `docs`, or the subfolder chosen when docs/ already serves a documentation site. `{{extra-never-write}}` lists the folders of any Spec Kit, OpenSpec or Kiro setup found, written as `, openspec/ or .kiro/specs/`, and is empty when there are none.\n\nThe block holds the workflow and where memory lives, never project knowledge; that goes in docs/.\n---\nproduct: \"{{product name}}\"\ndocs-format: 1\nissue-tracker: \"{{address a ticket key is appended to, such as https://example.atlassian.net/browse/}}\"\n---\n# {{Product name}}\n\n## What it is\n<!-- required: who uses the product and for what, in 2 to 4 sentences. Not a feature list. -->\n\n## Domains\n<!-- required, at least one row: docs-init asks for it. spec-start and docs-map add a row the moment a new domain is named.\nThe owner is who says go for that domain; on a solo project, that is you. A domain's behavior lives at behavior/<domain>/. -->\n| Domain | Covers | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{domain}} | {{what it covers}} | {{person or team}} |\n\n## Behavior\nSee [behavior/](behavior/): one folder per domain, one file per capability, each a short list of claims with IDs.\n\n## Architecture\nSee [architecture/](architecture/): one file per area, `stack.md` first.\n---\narea: stack\n---\n# Stack\n\n<!-- Current state only. The why lives in decision records.\ndocs-init writes Commands. docs-map adds Languages and frameworks when a domain needs it. -->\n\n## Languages and frameworks\n<!-- optional until docs-map fills it -->\n| Name | Version | Used for |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{name}} | {{version}} | {{what it's used for}} |\n\n## Commands\n<!-- spec-build and spec-ship run these, so keep them exact. Delete a row the project has no command for. -->\n| Task | Command |\n| --- | --- |\n| Install | {{command}} |\n| Run | {{command}} |\n| Test | {{command}} |\n| Lint | {{command}} |\n| Build | {{command}} |\n<!-- project-memory:start · managed by docs-init; edit outside these markers -->\n## Project memory\n- Start every task at {{docs-path}}/index.md, or at the active spec's tasks.md on a spec\n  branch, and load only what they link to. Load glossary.md when naming things and\n  decisions/ before changing a lasting choice.\n- Answer what the product does from {{docs-path}}/behavior/; open the code only to change it.\n- Every code change belongs to a spec in {{docs-path}}/specs/. None yet: start one (spec-start).\n- One branch per spec, named after its slug. The active spec is the one matching the current branch.\n- Every session adds its line to tasks.md. If something changes mid-way, update spec.md\n  or plan.md, then recheck every task.\n- Write specs, plans, tasks, glossary terms and decisions into {{docs-path}}/,\n  never into SPEC.md, tasks/, CONTEXT.md or docs/superpowers/{{extra-never-write}}.\n- Before opening a pull request, ship the spec (spec-ship); the PR title starts with the slug.\n<!-- project-memory:end -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
