{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nroot = Path.cwd()\nfor directory in reversed((root, *root.parents)):\n    candidate = directory / 'AGENTS.md'\n    if candidate.is_file():\n        print(json.dumps({'path': str(candidate), 'content': candidate.read_text()}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"path\": \"/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/AGENTS.md\", \"content\": \"# Maandly Workspace \\u2014 Agent Instructions\\n\\nUse this file when working from `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects`.\\n\\n## Workspace Scope\\n\\nThis workspace contains two application repos and one product-docs repo:\\n\\n| Repo | Purpose |\\n| ---- | ------- |\\n| `maandly-backend/` | Backend API contract, auth, payments, persistence |\\n| `maandly-frontend/` | Next.js web app consuming the backend contract |\\n| `maandly-product/` | Canonical product docs, rules, feature specs, architecture, decisions, research, and planning docs |\\n\\nIf the task is implementation work inside one repo, switch into that repo and follow its local `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\\nFor implementation, run commands from that repo root so repo-local settings and skills are active.\\n\\nUse the workspace root only for:\\n- Cross-repo planning\\n- Shared feature/status updates in `maandly-product/docs`\\n- Product and architecture documentation in `maandly-product/docs`\\n- Coordinating backend-first, frontend-second work\\n\\nUse the workspace-level `docs-governance` skill when the task is primarily about shared docs, docs sync, or deciding between shared and repo-local docs.\\nBefore creating, moving, or reorganizing shared docs, read `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md` and follow its folder ownership matrix.\\nFor cross-repo features, keep the shared feature doc handoff section current so frontend can start from documented backend state instead of inferring intent from code alone.\\n\\n## Shared Documentation Source Of Truth\\n\\nThese shared docs are authoritative across both repos:\\n\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md`\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/features/*.md`\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/rules/*.md`\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md`\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/decisions/*.md`\\n- `/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/maandly-product/docs/architecture/**/*.md`\\n\\nRepo-local `docs/` folders are for technical implementation details only. They do not override shared product status, feature acceptance criteria, or business rules.\\n\\n## Priority Rules\\n\\n1. Shared `maandly-product/docs/rules/*.md` business rules\\n2. Shared `maandly-product/docs/features/*.md` feature specs\\n3. Repo-local `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`\\n4. Existing code patterns in the target repo\\n5. Your judgment if the above are silent\\n\\n## Before Starting Work\\n\\n1. Check shared `maandly-product/docs/STATUS.md`\\n2. Read `maandly-product/docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md` if the task creates, moves, or reorganizes docs\\n3. Read the relevant shared feature spec in `maandly-product/docs/features/`\\n4. Read applicable shared rules in `maandly-product/docs/rules/`\\n5. Read `maandly-product/docs/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md` for cross-repo workflow details\\n6. Switch into the target repo and read its local `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`\\n\\nIf a required feature spec does not exist, draft it and get approval before implementation.\\n\\n## Cross-Repo Execution\\n\\nWhen a feature spans both repos:\\n\\n1. Backend first, because the API is the contract\\n2. Frontend second, after the contract is clear\\n3. Keep API paths in sync: backend route \\u2194 `maandly-frontend/src/shared/lib/api/endpoints.ts`\\n4. Keep shared docs updated as each side progresses\\n5. Update repo-local technical docs only when implementation details changed\\n\\n## After Completing Work\\n\\n1. Mark completed acceptance criteria in the shared feature spec\\n2. Update shared `maandly-product/docs/STATUS.md`\\n3. Update repo-local technical docs if setup, architecture, API behavior, migrations, or troubleshooting changed\\n4. Report what was done and any open follow-ups\\n\\nDo not consider the task complete until documentation was updated or you explicitly state why no doc change was needed.\\n\"}\n{\"path\": \"/Users/yousefallaban/MyProjects/scrubjay-example/AGENTS.md\", \"content\": \"# Webshop\\n\\n<!-- project-memory:start \\u00b7 managed by docs-init; edit outside these markers -->\\n## Project memory\\n- Start every task at docs/index.md, or at the active spec's tasks.md on a spec\\n  branch, and load only what they link to. Load glossary.md when naming things and\\n  decisions/ before changing a lasting choice.\\n- Answer what the product does from docs/behavior/; open the code only to change it.\\n- Every code change belongs to a spec in docs/specs/. None yet: start one (spec-start).\\n- One branch per spec, named after its slug. The active spec is the one matching the current branch.\\n- Every session adds its line to tasks.md. If something changes mid-way, update spec.md\\n  or plan.md, then recheck every task.\\n- Write specs, plans, tasks, glossary terms and decisions into docs/,\\n  never into SPEC.md, tasks/, CONTEXT.md or docs/superpowers/.\\n- Before opening a pull request, ship the spec (spec-ship); the PR title starts with the slug.\\n<!-- project-memory:end -->\\n\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
